    "type": "ICQ",
    "module": "Module6",
    "source": "M6 Lesson 5 · In-Content Questions · arp-icq-260",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>Previously, you were told that Everton Ltd owns 80% of Speke Ltd and 40% of Anfield Ltd. Now assume that Anfield sold goods to Everton for £50,000, making a margin of 20%. At 31 December 20X4, the year end, Everton holds half of these goods in its storeroom.</p><p>What is the unrealised profit?</p>",
    "a": "<p>The unrealised profit is calculated as:</p><p>£50,000 x 20% (margin) x ½ x 40% (group share) = £2,000</p><p>The required journal entry to eliminate the unrealised profit is as follows:</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Account name</td><td class=\"num\">£</td><td class=\"num\">£</td></tr><tr><td>Dr</td><td class=\"num\">Share of profit of Anfield</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>2,000</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Cr</td><td class=\"num\">Inventory</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>2,000</p><p>Being the elimination of the unrealised profit</p><p>Previously, in the consolidated SPL, the share of profit of the associate was £28,000. Now it is £26,000 (£28,000 – unrealised profit of £2,000).</p>",
    "isHTML": true,
    "linkTags": [
      "associates-unrealised-profit"
    ],
    "lesson": "Lesson5"
