    "lesson": "Lesson7",
    "appendix": {
      "title": "Case information",
      "html": "<p>Consolidation of a foreign subsidiary</p><p>Worldwide plc (Worldwide) purchased 75,000 CA$1 shares in a Canadian company, Maple Ltd (Maple), for £360,000 on 1 January 20X3. Review the extracts from the statement of financial position of Maple at that date.</p><p>Maple Ltd</p><p>Statement of financial position (extracts)</p><p>As at 1 January 20X3</p><p>CA$’000</p><p>Equity</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Share capital</td><td class=\"num\">100</td></tr><tr><td>Retained earnings</td><td class=\"num\">560</td></tr><tr><td>Total equity</td><td class=\"num\">660</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The abbreviated statements of financial position and extracts from the statements of profit or loss of the two companies at 31 December 20X3 were as follows:</p><p>Statements of financial position (abbreviated)</p><p>As at 31 December 20X3</p><p>Worldwide</p><p>Maple</p><p>£’000</p><p>CA$’000</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Non-current assets</td><td class=\"num\">180</td><td class=\"num\">170</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Investment in Maple</td><td class=\"num\">360</td><td class=\"num\">-</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Other net assets</td><td class=\"num\">250</td><td class=\"num\">530</td><td class=\"num\">790</td><td class=\"num\">700</td></tr><tr><td>Share capital</td><td class=\"num\">150</td><td class=\"num\">100</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><td>Retained earnings</td><td class=\"num\">640</td><td class=\"num\">600</td><td class=\"num\">790</td><td class=\"num\">700</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Statements of profit or loss (extracts)</p><p>For the year ended 31 December 20X3</p><p>Worldwide</p><p>Maple</p><p>£’000</p><p>CA$’000</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Profit before income taxes</td><td class=\"num\">81</td><td class=\"num\">86</td></tr><tr><td>Income tax expense</td><td class=\"num\">(20)</td><td class=\"num\">(21)</td></tr><tr><td>PROFIT FOR THE YEAR</td><td class=\"num\">61</td><td class=\"num\">65</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Maple paid a dividend of CA$25,000 during the year, when the exchange rate was CA$1.63. Dividends received from Maple are included in dividend income.</p><p>Following an impairment review in the current year, 20% of the recognised goodwill must be written off. NCI is based on share of net assets.</p><p>The relevant exchange rates are as follows:</p><p>1 January 20X3 – CA$1.60: £1</p><p>Average for 20X3 – CA$1.63: £1</p><p>31 December 20X3 – CA$1.65: £1</p><p>Required:</p><p>Construct, showing all workings, the Worldwide Group’s consolidated statement of financial position as at 31 December 20X3 and the consolidated statement of profit or loss for the year ended.</p><p>Construct, showing all workings, the Worldwide Group’s consolidated statement of other comprehensive income for the year ended 31 December 20X3.</p>"
    }
