    "source": "M6 Lesson 6 · In-Content Questions · arp-icq-267",
    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>Moritz plc (Moritz) is one of five investors sharing control of Ronda Ltd (Ronda). Each of the five investors has a 20% shareholding in Ronda.</p><p>Goods costing £200,000 were sold for £300,000 during the year ended 30 June 20X3. Half of the goods remain in inventories at 30 June 20X3.</p><p>Assuming that Moritz sells to Ronda, the effect on the financial statements of Moritz will be:</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><div><span>Adjust cost of sales upwards by 10 and investment in Ronda downwards by 10</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><div><span>Adjust cost of sales downwards by 10 and investment in Ronda upwards by 10</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><div><span>Adjust cost of sales upwards by 50 and investment in Ronda downwards by 50</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><div><span>Adjust cost of sales downwards by 50 and investment in Ronda upwards by 50</span></div></div><p>Assuming that Ronda sells to Moritz, the effect on the financial statements of Moritz will be:</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><div><span>Adjust share of profits of joint venture downwards by 10 and inventories upwards by 10</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><div><span>Adjust share of profits of joint venture downwards by 10 and inventories downwards by 10</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><div><span>Adjust cost of sales downwards by 10 and inventories upwards by 10</span></div></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><div><span>Adjust cost of sales downwards by 10 and inventories downwards by 10</span></div></div>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is a.</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td class=\"num\">300</td></tr><tr><td>Cost of sales</td><td class=\"num\">(200)</td></tr><tr><td>Gross profit</td><td class=\"num\">100</td></tr><tr><td>Unrealised profit (50%)</td><td class=\"num\">50</td></tr><tr><td>Group share (20%)</td><td class=\"num\">10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>This is a downstream transaction (group sells goods to joint venture).</p><p>If Moritz sells goods to Ronda, then its profits are overstated at the year end. This is adjusted for by debiting cost of sales (with the group share only).</p><p>Inventories of Ronda are not consolidated (since Ronda is a joint venture and equity accounting is applied) so cannot be reduced directly in the consolidated financial statements. Instead, we reduce the investment in the joint venture as this includes the group’s share of inventories of Ronda.</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Dr</td><td class=\"num\">SPL – cost of sales</td><td class=\"num\">10</td></tr><tr><td>Cr</td><td class=\"num\">Investment in Ronda</td><td class=\"num\">10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Being elimination of intercompany unrealised profit</p><p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is b.</p><p>This is an upstream transaction (joint venture sells goods to group).</p><p>If Ronda sells goods to Moritz (an upstream transaction), then Moritz’s inventories are overstated at the year end so must be reduced in the consolidated financial statements to eliminate the group share of unrealised profit.</p><p>Profits of Ronda are not consolidated (since Ronda is a joint venture and equity accounting is applied) so we cannot adjust cost of sales. We instead reduce the share of the joint venture’s profit as this includes a share of cost of sales.</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><caption><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span><span class=\"source-table-heading\">£’000</span></caption><tbody><tr><td>Dr</td><td class=\"num\">SPL – share of profit of joint venture</td><td class=\"num\">10</td></tr><tr><td>Cr</td><td class=\"num\">Inventories</td><td class=\"num\">10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Being elimination of intercompany unrealised profit in inventories</p>",
